WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.268 --> 00:00:07.171
On Valentine's Day 2022,

00:00:07.204 --> 00:00:12.043
a pontoon bridge appeared
near the border of Belarus and Ukraine.

00:00:12.743 --> 00:00:15.713
One day, an empty river,

00:00:15.746 --> 00:00:18.416
and the next day, a bridge.

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:22.386
I’m the cofounder
of an Earth imaging company,

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.587
and with our satellites,

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:26.657
we can see the entire world every day.

00:00:27.191 --> 00:00:30.261
And from space, we were able
to detect that bridge,

00:00:30.261 --> 00:00:31.462
zoom in,

00:00:31.495 --> 00:00:35.566
and that picture was broadcast
around the world the next morning.

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:39.537
Everyone could see
that something was changing.

00:00:41.105 --> 00:00:44.542
And then ten days later,
Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:49.480
Thanks to satellite imagery,
many governments and NGOs,

00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:51.582
researchers and journalists,

00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:55.519
they all had access
to the same daily facts,

00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:57.988
the same baseline of reality,

00:00:58.022 --> 00:01:01.192
and the same possibility,
at least in theory,

00:01:01.225 --> 00:01:03.828
of seeing clearly enough
to respond together.

00:01:04.395 --> 00:01:06.230
And with that shared view of reality,

00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:09.400
we’re no longer arguing
if something is there

00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:12.303
but deciding what to do
because it is there.

00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:16.040
In the days that followed
that Valentine's Day bridge,

00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:20.144
Western nations coordinated
for severe sanctions against Russia

00:01:20.177 --> 00:01:22.413
and unified in their support for Ukraine.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.682
But for months beforehand,

00:01:24.715 --> 00:01:27.418
we saw an increase of military activity

00:01:27.451 --> 00:01:29.653
and tanks amassing at the border.

00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:32.389
The signals were there.

00:01:33.324 --> 00:01:36.994
Perhaps the allies stopped
the worst from happening,

00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:38.629
but they didn't stop the war.

00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:43.067
And I sat with that
for a really long time.

00:01:44.335 --> 00:01:47.872
The satellites, they worked
exactly as they were designed.

00:01:47.872 --> 00:01:49.440
They showed the emerging threat.

00:01:49.473 --> 00:01:51.008
They saw the threat.

00:01:51.575 --> 00:01:54.845
But the institutions
that were supposed to respond,

00:01:54.879 --> 00:01:56.514
they weren't built for this.

00:01:57.381 --> 00:02:00.885
The alliances, the frameworks,
the coordination mechanisms,

00:02:00.918 --> 00:02:03.888
they weren't built
to handle signal at this speed

00:02:03.921 --> 00:02:06.223
or to incorporate
this amount of information.

00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:10.427
And we built this extraordinary eye,

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:14.165
an independent source of truth
about what's happening on the planet.

00:02:14.665 --> 00:02:18.969
But an eye that's not connected
to a functional nervous system

00:02:19.003 --> 00:02:22.173
and a body capable of response,

00:02:22.206 --> 00:02:24.008
that eye is just a witness.

00:02:24.608 --> 00:02:28.512
But fortunately, new technologies
are helping to close that gap.

00:02:28.546 --> 00:02:31.415
When you take all of this earth data

00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:35.152
and pair it with
the analytical power of AI,

00:02:35.152 --> 00:02:38.722
we can build extremely different things,

00:02:38.756 --> 00:02:41.825
action in an entirely new way.

00:02:42.426 --> 00:02:46.197
We're entering into an era
that we call planetary intelligence,

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.833
where new capabilities in action
can happen at the speed of change.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:54.338
Now, my cofounder, Will,
was on this spot in 2014,

00:02:54.338 --> 00:02:56.307
and he shared with you all our dream.

00:02:56.807 --> 00:03:00.211
What if we could image
the whole world every day?

00:03:01.212 --> 00:03:04.381
And he came back in 2018 with a new dream.

00:03:04.415 --> 00:03:08.018
What if we can use AI to understand
how the world is changing?

00:03:09.086 --> 00:03:12.323
And today, that vision
is becoming a reality.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.758
And before I share that with you today,

00:03:14.758 --> 00:03:16.894
I want to provide a little bit of context.

00:03:17.461 --> 00:03:20.364
The space sector is going
through a renaissance right now.

00:03:20.397 --> 00:03:23.667
We have reusable rockets,
thousands of satellites.

00:03:24.235 --> 00:03:28.005
And for the first time in over 50 years,

00:03:28.038 --> 00:03:30.174
we just sent humans to the moon and back.

00:03:30.574 --> 00:03:34.044
NASA is inspiring us once again
with this picture

00:03:34.044 --> 00:03:36.914
to gain perspective
that we live on this beautiful,

00:03:36.947 --> 00:03:39.617
precious spaceship Earth
that we call home.

00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:44.054
And with hundreds of satellites
that are all monitoring the planet,

00:03:44.054 --> 00:03:46.123
they're getting connected to each other,

00:03:46.156 --> 00:03:48.659
and we're putting
a lot more compute next to it.

00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:51.595
It's beginning to build
a planetary nervous system.

00:03:52.963 --> 00:03:54.565
And here on the ground,

00:03:54.565 --> 00:03:59.570
we're all in amazement as AI just
continues to accelerate at rapid speed.

00:04:00.404 --> 00:04:02.039
And like many of you here,

00:04:02.072 --> 00:04:04.408
I'm holding on to that polarity

00:04:04.441 --> 00:04:07.611
between the sheer awesomeness
of this technology,

00:04:07.645 --> 00:04:09.313
and also a bit of anxiety

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:12.016
about how this comes
into the world in the right way.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.486
We have to get governance right,

00:04:15.486 --> 00:04:17.488
and we have to get alignment right.

00:04:17.821 --> 00:04:20.658
For AI to work for everyone

00:04:20.691 --> 00:04:23.527
and the larger living world,

00:04:23.527 --> 00:04:26.697
we need it to speak the language
of the planetary systems

00:04:26.697 --> 00:04:28.299
to which we're all embedded.

00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:33.003
It must understand our infrastructure
and human activity,

00:04:33.037 --> 00:04:39.143
but also the impacts on the water,
the trees and the soil.

00:04:39.777 --> 00:04:42.079
So let me show you what this looks like.

00:04:43.013 --> 00:04:46.283
So when you combine all of this Earth data

00:04:46.317 --> 00:04:49.086
with AI and large language models,

00:04:49.119 --> 00:04:53.424
we are allowing for global change
to happen in near real time.

00:04:53.457 --> 00:04:55.726
You can see change
in just about everywhere

00:04:55.759 --> 00:04:58.529
over vast distances and time.

00:04:59.263 --> 00:05:03.901
It's helping to close that gap
between awareness and action.

00:05:04.268 --> 00:05:07.938
A farmer can understand
how healthy their soil is.

00:05:08.238 --> 00:05:11.909
An insurer can create a dynamic
and custom policy

00:05:11.909 --> 00:05:15.346
based on the real-time
environmental risk of the asset.

00:05:15.346 --> 00:05:17.114
And a finance minister,

00:05:17.147 --> 00:05:21.552
they can account for the true cost
of their financial economy

00:05:21.585 --> 00:05:25.055
along with their rich,
living, natural ecosystems.

00:05:25.422 --> 00:05:29.460
So planetary intelligence
guides our actions

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.694
much in the same way

00:05:30.728 --> 00:05:34.898
that the eye connected
to a nervous system guides the body

00:05:34.932 --> 00:05:39.436
so that humanity is no longer a witness
to what's happening.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.440
We can become stewards
for the planet and our society.

00:05:44.041 --> 00:05:46.844
And we're already seeing glimmers
of planetary intelligence

00:05:46.877 --> 00:05:48.679
happening all over the world.

00:05:48.712 --> 00:05:51.849
It is already measuring
global change in near real time,

00:05:51.882 --> 00:05:55.219
guiding human intervention
where it's needed the most.

00:05:55.252 --> 00:05:57.054
So let me show you a few examples.

00:05:57.087 --> 00:05:58.889
First, let's go to Brazil.

00:05:58.922 --> 00:06:01.658
The Brazilian Amazon is huge.

00:06:01.692 --> 00:06:03.527
It's five million square kilometers,

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.530
roughly two thirds the size
of the United States,

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.633
and it's brimming with rich biodiversity,

00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:12.136
countless Indigenous communities.

00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:16.707
And it's the home of about 20 percent
of the planet's freshwater supply.

00:06:17.608 --> 00:06:20.544
But deep in the dense
forests of the Amazon,

00:06:20.577 --> 00:06:24.114
there are illegal activities
that are happening all the time.

00:06:24.148 --> 00:06:27.551
Fields are cleared for illicit crops.

00:06:27.584 --> 00:06:30.254
Runways are cut for narco traffickers.

00:06:30.754 --> 00:06:34.758
Riverbeds are illegally mined
and poisoning downstream communities.

00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:37.594
And deforestation still happens every day.

00:06:37.895 --> 00:06:39.329
So how do you stop that?

00:06:40.097 --> 00:06:43.300
You can't manually patrol that
with boots on the ground

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.935
and planes and paperwork.

00:06:45.936 --> 00:06:49.673
So our team worked with local partners
and the Brazilian federal police

00:06:49.706 --> 00:06:53.777
to create a system that monitors
the entire Brazilian Amazon every day.

00:06:54.244 --> 00:06:57.481
And it looks for a signal
of illegal activity.

00:06:57.481 --> 00:06:59.983
For instance, an unpermitted road.

00:07:00.951 --> 00:07:05.422
And today, over 100 000 people
across the Brazilian government,

00:07:05.456 --> 00:07:07.958
from a ranger to federal courts,

00:07:07.958 --> 00:07:09.693
they use this system

00:07:09.693 --> 00:07:11.628
and over the last three years,

00:07:11.662 --> 00:07:15.699
they’ve seized four billion dollars’ worth
of illegal equipment in the Amazon.

00:07:15.732 --> 00:07:17.201
And most importantly, I think,

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:20.471
over wherever this was deployed,

00:07:20.471 --> 00:07:24.074
deforestation rates decreased
by over 50 percent.

00:07:24.541 --> 00:07:29.847
(Applause)

00:07:29.847 --> 00:07:32.783
Now let's see what this looks like
at the speed of change.

00:07:32.816 --> 00:07:34.218
Let's go to Kenya.

00:07:34.251 --> 00:07:38.622
A herder has kept his cattle
on the same semi-arid land

00:07:38.622 --> 00:07:40.424
for generations.

00:07:40.457 --> 00:07:43.794
And livestock to pastoral families
is not just their income,

00:07:43.827 --> 00:07:46.363
it's their savings, their insurance,

00:07:46.396 --> 00:07:48.699
the accumulated wealth of a lifetime.

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:51.168
But every few years, the rains fail.

00:07:51.602 --> 00:07:53.237
And when they do,

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:54.738
the grass dries up,

00:07:54.771 --> 00:07:57.341
the cattle weaken and they start to die.

00:07:57.641 --> 00:08:01.478
So one bad drought can wipe out
the economic foundation of a family

00:08:01.512 --> 00:08:02.779
in a matter of weeks.

00:08:03.447 --> 00:08:06.783
But now, a new drought insurance
program is coming together.

00:08:07.384 --> 00:08:10.320
The satellite is able to read
the health of the grass.

00:08:10.354 --> 00:08:13.090
If that health falls
below a critical threshold,

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.459
an automatic payment is sent
via mobile money

00:08:15.459 --> 00:08:18.161
to every pastoralist
in the region affected

00:08:18.161 --> 00:08:21.265
so that they can go and buy
supplemental food for their animals.

00:08:21.765 --> 00:08:24.801
So the herder doesn't need
to understand satellite imagery.

00:08:24.835 --> 00:08:27.104
He doesn't even need to file a claim.

00:08:28.171 --> 00:08:30.874
Satellite reads the grass,
a number crosses a line,

00:08:30.874 --> 00:08:32.643
money appears on his phone,

00:08:32.643 --> 00:08:36.079
he moves his herd,
he buys supplemental food,

00:08:36.113 --> 00:08:39.650
and the crisis that would
have unfolded doesn't.

00:08:40.584 --> 00:08:44.254
Over a million and a half herders
across the Horn of Africa

00:08:44.288 --> 00:08:47.024
are now protected with this
drought insurance program.

00:08:47.057 --> 00:08:51.695
(Applause)

00:08:51.728 --> 00:08:53.130
So this is what it looks like

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.867
when you use a signal from space
to guide human action

00:08:57.234 --> 00:08:59.469
in real time to changing events.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.707
The eye detects change
and the body moves to prevent harm.

00:09:05.309 --> 00:09:08.412
And I think there's something
deeper going on here.

00:09:09.112 --> 00:09:13.717
Planetary intelligence
doesn't just change what we do,

00:09:13.717 --> 00:09:16.553
but it changes how we know the world

00:09:16.587 --> 00:09:18.121
and our place within it.

00:09:19.056 --> 00:09:21.792
It allows for us to see
with the whole in mind.

00:09:22.593 --> 00:09:27.197
And dissolves the false separation
between our culture and our society

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.333
and that of the larger living planet.

00:09:30.634 --> 00:09:32.636
And we're living through a time right now

00:09:32.669 --> 00:09:35.606
where many of our institutions
and our alliances

00:09:35.606 --> 00:09:38.041
are fracturing and falling apart.

00:09:38.709 --> 00:09:41.845
And this is extremely painful

00:09:41.845 --> 00:09:43.013
because the problems

00:09:43.046 --> 00:09:46.183
that these institutions
were built to address

00:09:46.216 --> 00:09:47.884
are only intensifying.

00:09:48.218 --> 00:09:50.721
But I believe that planetary intelligence

00:09:50.721 --> 00:09:53.724
can help us transform our institutions.

00:09:54.958 --> 00:09:58.962
Purpose-built for the speed
and the complexity of the 21st century.

00:10:00.097 --> 00:10:03.433
We can all build new
products and institutions

00:10:03.433 --> 00:10:06.370
that allow for us
to see change in real time.

00:10:06.403 --> 00:10:10.207
And it can transform just
about every sector of our society,

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.410
from finance to infrastructure,

00:10:13.443 --> 00:10:17.247
decision-making
and accountability mechanisms,

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.383
all at the speed of change,

00:10:19.383 --> 00:10:22.052
in order for us to build
a more resilient future

00:10:22.085 --> 00:10:25.989
so that the next time
tanks amass at a border,

00:10:26.023 --> 00:10:28.158
there will be no pontoon bridge.

00:10:29.526 --> 00:10:33.130
I started my career believing
that information would save us.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:37.401
I now know that only
coordination actually will.

00:10:38.669 --> 00:10:40.704
We gave the earth eyes.

00:10:41.438 --> 00:10:43.407
We're connecting it to the brain.

00:10:43.807 --> 00:10:48.378
But now, now the only thing left
to do is to build the body,

00:10:48.412 --> 00:10:52.215
the trust, the alliances,
the institutions,

00:10:52.249 --> 00:10:55.218
that is brave enough to move
when the mind signals.

00:10:56.319 --> 00:10:57.554
Thank you.

00:10:57.587 --> 00:11:04.461
(Applause)

00:11:04.494 --> 00:11:07.531
DS: Thank you so much
for watching Robbie’s incredible TED Talk.

00:11:07.564 --> 00:11:09.733
I'm Divya Siddharth,
one of the guest curators

00:11:09.766 --> 00:11:11.802
for Robbie’s session
this year at TED2026,

00:11:11.802 --> 00:11:13.937
along with the incredible Audrey Tang.

00:11:14.504 --> 00:11:16.606
And I think the reason we were so excited

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.408
to share Robbie's work with the world

00:11:18.442 --> 00:11:21.278
is because we think it's a huge part
of what the world needs

00:11:21.278 --> 00:11:23.980
to collectively govern
and understand our future with AI.

00:11:24.014 --> 00:11:27.084
One of the reasons this is an important
talk to have on stage now

00:11:27.084 --> 00:11:29.786
is information is power.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.988
And the incredible thing
that Planet has done

00:11:32.022 --> 00:11:34.491
is build a very powerful
information source

00:11:34.524 --> 00:11:38.261
and make it, in as much as they can,
available to everyone.

00:11:38.295 --> 00:11:40.363
And so they not only
create the information,

00:11:40.363 --> 00:11:41.598
which lots of people do,

00:11:41.631 --> 00:11:43.734
but they actually
let people benefit from it.

00:11:43.767 --> 00:11:45.936
And that's, in the age of AI,
not always true.

00:11:45.969 --> 00:11:48.872
Audrey Tang: When you see the Earth
from the outer space,

00:11:48.905 --> 00:11:50.474
we become better people

00:11:50.507 --> 00:11:55.512
because we can then imagine
that we're on this fragile spaceship.

00:11:55.545 --> 00:11:58.648
And that really changed me
to want to wage peace

00:11:58.682 --> 00:12:01.685
much more forcefully than we wage war.

